line	<str>Fight the first 3 forms of Koschei the Deathless without weapons, armour, or runes. (You can pray flick him for the first 3 forms. Dying in the room is safe, even for regular Hardcore Ironmen). Do not go up the ladder after completing the 3rd form - it is safe to die from the 4th form.</str>
line	
line	<str>You can choose to let the 4th form kill you (this is safe for Group Hardcore Ironmen as Koschei will not actually finish you in this form; the player will faint and wake up upstairs rather than being killed), or you can kill it (slower and is not necessary).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Thorvald again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Peer the Seer south-west of the market.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the door to his house, south-west of the market (with a green bed), and read the riddle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Each line of the riddle gives you one letter of a four-letter word. See the table below for the first riddle line and the related answer.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the door again and climb-up the ladder.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search/study these objects to get a bucket, red disk, wooden disk, jug, and red herring:</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the red herring on the cooking range.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sticky red goop on the wooden disk.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Open the trapdoor on the east side, climb-down the trapdoor, and use the two red disks on the <col=800000>abstract mural</col>.</col>
step	57	-	Quick guide step 57
line	<str>Talk to Brundt in the longhall to start the quest. (Fairy ring DKS and run south-west to Rellekka) , or if started or finished Mountain Daughter</str>
line	
line	<str>The trials may be done in any order, however this quick guide will show you the fastest order.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Manni the Reveller while in the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the  keg of beer and challenge Manni to a drinking contest. You will lose.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you did not bring a beer, grab the beer tankard now.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sigli the Huntsman outside, near the entrance of the longhall, to obtain the Hunters' Talisman.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Olaf the Bard just east of the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Olaf again.</str>
line	
line	<str>To get a lyre, either make it yourself (Requires 25 Fletching 40 Woodcutting 40 Crafting and 6 free inventory spaces) or kill Lanzig (1/17 drop rate). Killing lanzig takes longer on average. You must enchant it either way.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport to Camelot or walk to Seers' Village.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you are making the lyre yourself:</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Seers' Village pub and talk to the Poison Salesman to buy a low alcohol keg for 250 coins.</str>
line	
line	<str>Buy a regular beer if you forgot to take a beer tankard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a Rellekka house teleport to return, or simply walk back. If walking, left-click on your talisman to check if The Draugen is nearby on your way. If so, kill him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the beer, or beer tankard, on the council workman by the bridge south of Rellekka to obtain strange object.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go north across the bridge, then walk a bit west until you see a small narrow path heading south into the water. (The large rib cage sticking out of the water on the left side of the bridge)</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your raw shark/manta ray/sea turtle on the strange altar to enchant your lyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow your talisman by left-clicking on it and kill The Draugen now if you haven't already. Appears as a grey butterfly before locating the correct tile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once done, head back into Rellekka and talk to Sigli at the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the outside of the longhall to the pipe on the eastern wall. Use a tinderbox on your strange object and use the lit strange object on the pipe.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the north-eastern back door of the longhall, walk onto the stage, and play your enchanted lyre.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the back door, enter the main long hall, and take a keg of beer off the table.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your low alcohol keg on the keg of beer.</str>
line	
line	<str>Challenge Manni to a drinking contest again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sigmund The Merchant in the market west of the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Sailor on the docks to the north-west.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Olaf the Bard just east of the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Yrsa at the clothing store west of the market.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Brundt the Chieftain in the longhall. or if you are doing or have finished Mountain Daughter</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Sigli the Huntsman just south of the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Skulgrimen in the hut just north of the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Fisherman north of the market.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Swensen the Navigator in the building south of the market.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Swensen again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the ladder and take the South, West, East, North, South, East, then North portals. Climb up the ladder.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Peer the Seer just north-west of Swensen.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Thorvald the Warrior in the hut just north of the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Manni the Reveller in the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Thora the Barkeep in the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Askeladden in front of the longhall, pay him 5,000 coins.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head back and talk to (in order):</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to a bank (The Seers' Village bank is close) and deposit all of your items (you cannot have any weapons, armour, or runes).</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring equipment for the fight:</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Thorvald just north of the longhall.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the ladder. If you have a knife and dramen branch, cut it into a staff and equip it. You can also use celastrus bark to fletch a battlestaff.</str>
line	
line	<str>Fight the first 3 forms of Koschei the Deathless without weapons, armour, or runes. (You can pray flick him for the first 3 forms. Dying in the room is safe, even for regular Hardcore Ironmen). Do not go up the ladder after completing the 3rd form - it is safe to die from the 4th form.</str>
line	
line	<str>You can choose to let the 4th form kill you (this is safe for Group Hardcore Ironmen as Koschei will not actually finish you in this form; the player will faint and wake up upstairs rather than being killed), or you can kill it (slower and is not necessary).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Thorvald again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Peer the Seer south-west of the market.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the door to his house, south-west of the market (with a green bed), and read the riddle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Each line of the riddle gives you one letter of a four-letter word. See the table below for the first riddle line and the related answer.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the door again and climb-up the ladder.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search/study these objects to get a bucket, red disk, wooden disk, jug, and red herring:</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the red herring on the cooking range.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the sticky red goop on the wooden disk.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the trapdoor on the east side, climb-down the trapdoor, and use the two red disks on the abstract mural.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Return upstairs and use the bucket on the tap by the cooking range.</col>
